(EPIDEMICS) Tj T*
(When you draw an Epidemic card: increase the infection rate by one step, draw the) Tj T*
(bottom card of the infection deck and put 3 cubes on that city, then shuffle the) Tj T*
(infection discard pile and put it on top of the infection deck.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(OUTBREAKS) Tj T*
(If a city would get a 4th cube of one color, there is an outbreak instead: put 1 cube) Tj T*
(of that color on every connected city and move the outbreak marker. Outbreaks can) Tj T*
(chain, but each city has at most one outbreak per chain.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(HAND LIMIT) Tj T*
(Each player may hold at most 7 cards. Discard or play event cards immediately if you) Tj T*
(have more. Event cards can be played at any time and do not cost an action.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(ERADICATION) Tj T*
(A disease is eradicated when it is cured and no cube of that color is left on the) Tj T*
(board. Cities of that color are no longer infected.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(ROLES) Tj T*
(- Medic: removes all cubes of one color when treating; cured diseases vanish where the) Tj T*
(   Medic is.) Tj T*
(- Scientist: needs only 4 cards of the same color to discover a cure.) Tj T*
(- Researcher: may give any city card when sharing knowledge.) Tj T*
(- Operations Expert: builds a research station without discarding a card.) Tj T*
(- Dispatcher: may move other players' pawns.) Tj T*
(- Quarantine Specialist: prevents cube placement in its city and the connected cities.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(WINNING AND LOSING) Tj T*
(The team wins immediately when all 4 cures are discovered. The team loses if there are) Tj T*
(8 outbreaks, if a disease runs out of cubes, or if the player deck runs out when a) Tj T*
(player must draw.) Tj T*
ET
